# Font binaries recovered from the synthetic fixture's build. Regenerate with:
#   python -m gdl.fonts tests/data/synthetic/synthetic.gdl gdl/fonts/
#
# Ignored per file rather than as a class: the files do not share a license.
# Open Sans is Apache 2.0 and declares it in its own name table, so it is
# tracked; so is the design systems' own Open Sans (opensans-latin.woff2, not
# recovered but Google Fonts' own, SIL OFL 1.1, LICENSE-OpenSans-OFL.txt).
# Arial and Arial Black are retail Monotype faces, and the Extron icon fonts
# carry no license grant at all. gdl/fonts/README.md has the per-file detail,
# read from each font rather than assumed.
#
# This ignore does not keep the bytes out of git - every face is embedded in
# the tracked synthetic build or a seed, and is recoverable from it exactly. It
# prevents a second, more conveniently redistributable copy, nothing more.
#
# Without the untracked faces the harness degrades: each draws in a stand-in -
# the host's copy, or the recovered Arial - and tests/score.py record refuses
# to score over one (gdl/fonts/README.md).
gdl/fonts/*
!gdl/fonts/README.md
!gdl/fonts/LICENSE-OpenSans.txt
!gdl/fonts/opensans-regular.ttf
!gdl/fonts/opensans-light.ttf
!gdl/fonts/opensans-latin.woff2
!gdl/fonts/LICENSE-OpenSans-OFL.txt

# GUI Designer's own working files - its temp font folder (retail Monotype
# Arial and Arial Black, the same bytes the seeds embed) and its per-user
# settings - live in /private/ (below). Their old place stays ignored for a
# checkout that still holds it; gdl/fonts/README.md has the font policy.
/archive/gui-designer/

# Scratch output: extracted ProjectGCP, repacked .gdl, authored results.
out/

# New-GdlSeed.ps1 keeps its screenshot of the wizard in the temp folder. It is of
# the whole primary screen and must never reach a commit; ignored here in case
# one is copied into seeds/.
seeds/*-wizard.png

# Built viewer artifacts (regenerate with gdl.data + viewer/build_viewer.py).
panel-data.json
panel-atlas.html

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Extron's installed template library, copied here so the tests that read it
# need nothing on C:. Reinstallable with GUI Designer and ~470 MB, so it stays
# on disk but is not pushed; vendor/MANIFEST.md records exactly what belongs.
/vendor/*
!/vendor/README.md
!/vendor/MANIFEST.md

# On the owner's machine only, never tracked or published: GUI Designer's
# settings file and temp fonts, and the publish denylist (tools/public_sync.py).
/private/
